Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.589 align:start position:0%
 
if you're jumping into cana bridge of  spirits you may have noticed that the  game is more challenging than its cute  art style originally lets on to help out  we've got 13 tips and tricks to help you  be a better spirit guide  kana possesses an omnidirectional shield  that she can hold for a pretty long time  which in a pinch is a powerful defensive  measure but it's not one that you want  to rely on canis shield should be  considered a last resort something you  use when all else fails and you know  you're about to get hit this is because  the shield slows kana down  [Music]  early on this isn't too much of a  problem but after the opening hours of  the game you'll start facing groups of  enemies as well as more difficult mini  bosses and bosses all of which are both  fast and hit incredibly hard if your  shield takes too much damage it'll break  dealing you a big blow and sending you  flying so get into the habit of pairing  dodging and jumping to counter and avoid  enemy attacks parrying is an especially  crucial skill to get down and one that  can come in clutch later down the line  beyond defending kana can outright stop  certain attacks too kana's long-range  arsenal can knock enemies out of their  animations which will stop them from  using whatever attack they were  preparing using an arrow is the easiest  way to do so given the speed at which  kaina can fire one off however bombs can  typically work too  in bridge of spirits combat is hard and  the only way to really alleviate its  challenge is through kana's powerful rot  based abilities they are excellent for  dealing massive amounts of damage and  controlling the flow of battle to give  you some breathing room the only way to  use those abilities is by spending  courage which can most easily be  acquired in combat by dealing damage to  enemies spending courage is also the  only way you can heal during a fight too  so you need to be aggressive never back  off from a fight unless you absolutely  need to staying in the thick of combat  and weakening enemies is crucial for  building courage so you can both deal  the most damage and stay alive on  playstation 5 you can determine whether  you want to play bridge of spirits on  performance mode or fidelity mode the  former targets 60 fps at upscaled 4k  resolution while the latter locks the  frame rate at 30 fps at native 4k  resolution though fidelity mode makes  the game a whole lot prettier  performance mode is what you want it's  better from a combat perspective sure  the game won't be native 4k but you're  getting more frames per second and that  makes it a whole lot easier when you're  trying to time a parry or a dodge  kana has a just one more hit in your  finished state you can tell when you're  one hit away from death by looking at  the health bar it will be red and  flashing kana will always enter this  state before death so even if she only  has a tiny sliver of health left if it's  not red and blinking you have at least  one more hit before you're one hit away  from dying so to maximize the effects of  health items it's better to wait until  you've entered this state before healing  you can usually only heal a few times  each fight so just healing whenever is  not an ideal strategy wait until you  need to heal before deciding to heal  on playstation 5 the dual sense  controller will vibrate with a soft  heartbeat like frequency when you're  close to a hidden rod the frequency will  increase the closer to the rot you are  so while you're exploring be sure to  take stock of when your controller might  be trying to tell you something but you  don't need to find all of the rot you'll  have to discover at least 65 of them in  order to unlock all of cana's abilities  though kana's spirit pulse is primarily  a tool for solving puzzles lighting up  dark spaces and unlocking collectibles  it has offensive potential too most  notably it causes your bombs to explode  which helps if you don't want to wait  for the bombs to go off on their own or  you want to save your arrows  in most combat scenarios you'll have to  kill all the enemies in order to reveal  the source of the corruption and cleanse  the area you know you're done with  combat when enemies stop spawning  however there are a few moments where  you'll be put into a fight where there  are multiple points of corruption you'll  need to cleanse in these instances one  or two points can usually be cleansed  right from the start and they'll just  keep spawning enemies indefinitely until  you stop them try to get to these points  first and close them as quickly as  possible they usually spawn smaller  enemies that are meant to pester you and  distract you from the larger main threat  so getting rid of them early on will  make the fight so much easier  there is friendly fire in bridge's  spirits so even though that  unfortunately means that kana can damage  herself with her own bombs it also means  that the bigger enemies in the game  especially mini bosses and bosses can  damage and even kill smaller enemies so  if you're having trouble dealing with a  group of enemies try to angle a larger  enemy's attack to strike the smaller  enemies around them  the weak points on enemies mini bosses  and bosses are always marked in yellow  you have to shoot them with your bow as  they require a precise strike usually  that yellow is a crystallized chunk of  amber and shooting them will knock that  crystal off the enemy which transforms  into the gold energy that you or the rot  can collect to fill the courage gauge  and use your rot based abilities there  are a few instances where these weak  points can't be shot at immediately  though later on in the game you'll start  running into foes encased in thick armor  or rock and the only way to reveal their  weak points is to bomb them so if a  tough enemy doesn't seem to have a weak  spot try bombing them that will usually  reveal what you need to hit  [Music]  early on you'll unlock the ability to  have the rot interact with specific  flowers and the environment called  forest tiers transforming the rot into a  mass that can water crops clear  corruption and help solve certain  puzzles but it can be used as a weapon  too in instances where you can use that  ability in combat or use it outside of  combat and bring it to a fight go for it  both the spinning and slamming action  that the rock can do deal a lot of  damage be careful though as any hit  whether to kana or the rot will  immediately cause the rod to scatter so  get in as many hits as you can before  the enemy can touch you  you unlock a whole lot of in-game  currency throughout bridges spirits so  don't feel like you have to be frugal  when it comes to buying hats and masks  for your rot you will be swimming in  currency throughout the game even if you  don't spend a lot of time looking for  secrets and collectibles suspend at your  leisure you'll also earn plenty of carmo  points from killing enemies and doing  things like feeding fruit to the rod or  fixing statues in the environment which  you can then use to unlock new abilities  for kana at a fairly steady rate you  won't earn enough that you can just buy  whatever you want unless you plan on  searching off the beaten path and  completing optional quests you won't  finish the campaign with all of kana's  skills unlocked so if you're not down to  explore you do have to be a bit more  selective there but when it comes to  dressing the rot and cute outfits the  sky is the limit though a majority of  the puzzles in bridge of spirits are  pretty straightforward some both  mandatory and optional aren't in a few  cases the hints to a puzzle solution are  tied to the environment forcing you to  look at the world around kinah in order  to figure out what you need to do next  so if you're struggling on a puzzle look  at your immediate surroundings the clue  for a puzzle will always be right near  it so you won't have to go hunting for  information  hopefully those 13 pieces of advice help  you out how do you all feel about the  game leave your thoughts in the comments  section below be sure to subscribe to  gamespot if you're looking for more cana  bridges spirits content like our video  review and some master spirit difficulty  gameplay and be sure to like this video  if you found any of these tips helpful  or want to see us make more videos like  this for other games  you

